{
  "tema": 7181,
  "slug": "presencia-articulos",
  "titulo": "When Spanish needs the definite article el, la, los, las",
  "subtitulo": "El café mancha los dientes: Spanish uses the article where English doesn't.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Nouns used in a general sense as the subject need the article in Spanish: el café, la salud, los perros. English leaves it out.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Spanish and English don't use articles the same way. A very common mistake is leaving out **el, la, los, las** at the start of a sentence."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When a noun is the **subject** and you're talking about it **in general** (all coffee, health in general, whales as a species), Spanish **needs the article**; English doesn't."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "English",
            "Spanish"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "Coffee stains your teeth.",
              "**El** café mancha los dientes."
            ],
            [
              "Whales are mammals.",
              "**Las** ballenas son mamíferos."
            ],
            [
              "Health is more important than money.",
              "**La** salud es más importante que el dinero."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It also happens with abstract nouns (**la generosidad**, **el amor**) and with general likes: **me gusta el café**, **odio el tráfico**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: if English says it about everything of that kind, Spanish puts **el** or **la** in front."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==El café== cambia el color de los dientes.",
              "en": "Coffee changes the color of your teeth."
            },
            {
              "es": "==La cafeína== a veces provoca mareos.",
              "en": "Caffeine sometimes causes dizziness."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Los políticos== están discutiendo la reforma.",
              "en": "Politicians are discussing the reform."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Los latinoamericanos== tienen una cultura muy rica.",
              "en": "Latin Americans have a very rich culture."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Las ballenas== son mamíferos.",
              "en": "Whales are mammals."
            },
            {
              "es": "==La generosidad== es la mejor virtud.",
              "en": "Generosity is the best virtue."
            },
            {
              "es": "Me encanta ==el mar== en invierno.",
              "en": "I love the ocean in winter."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
